Subject: [PATCH] [mlir][dataflow] Revisit a terminator whose operands are all non-forwarded

LivenessAnalysis::visitBranchOperand gives a non-forwarded operand of a
RegionBranchTerminatorOpInterface the liveness of its parent's results,
read with getLatticeElement, which subscribes nothing. visitOperation
then subscribes the parent, not the terminator. A terminator with a
successor operand is subscribed to its parent's results by that
operand's meet, so it is visited again when one of them becomes live;
one whose operands are all non-forwarded never is. When the parent's
results become live only after the terminator was first visited (a
result of a private function that its caller reads), the operands stay
dead, and remove-dead-values erases the ops that define them, leaving
ub.poison in their place.

Each result's lattice now subscribes the point after the operand's owner
(addDependency), which is the terminator (or the branch op, for a
non-forwarded operand of its own).

---
diff --git a/mlir/lib/Analysis/DataFlow/LivenessAnalysis.cpp b/mlir/lib/Analysis/DataFlow/LivenessAnalysis.cpp
--- a/mlir/lib/Analysis/DataFlow/LivenessAnalysis.cpp
+++ b/mlir/lib/Analysis/DataFlow/LivenessAnalysis.cpp
@@ -153,9 +153,18 @@
   auto *visitOp =
       isa<RegionBranchTerminatorOpInterface>(op) ? op->getParentOp() : op;
   Liveness *operandLiveness[] = {getLatticeElement(operand.get())};
+  // The operand's liveness follows the results of `visitOp`, so `op`, the
+  // owner of the operand, must be visited again when one of them becomes
+  // live. For a terminator, `visitOperation` only subscribes `visitOp`
+  // itself: a terminator whose operands are all non-forwarded (none is a
+  // successor operand, whose meet would subscribe it) would never be
+  // visited again, and its operands would stay dead.
   SmallVector<const Liveness *, 4> resultsLiveness;
-  for (const Value result : visitOp->getResults())
-    resultsLiveness.push_back(getLatticeElement(result));
+  for (const Value result : visitOp->getResults()) {
+    Liveness *resultLiveness = getLatticeElement(result);
+    addDependency(resultLiveness, getProgramPointAfter(op));
+    resultsLiveness.push_back(resultLiveness);
+  }
   LDBG() << "Visiting operation for non-forwarded branch operand: "
          << OpWithFlags(visitOp, OpPrintingFlags().skipRegions());
   (void)visitOperation(visitOp, operandLiveness, resultsLiveness);
